this is a production of Cornell  University hello my name is Martha  Williams and I'm studying plant science  in the school of integrative plant  sciences because I love connections ever  since I was a little girl I used to see  how the plants in the soil  became the food that was on my dinner  table and as I've grown older I realized  that plants not only feed the body but  nourish the soul they bridge this gap  that we have between the technological  world we've created and the natural  world from which we have distanced  ourselves they build community for  example I had the opportunity this  summer to work with a handful of  children who work to plan and garden  plant this garden and maintain this  garden I watched how amazed they were  the same that they look at their  technology looking at the plants that  they were growing in the ground and I  saw how and all they were that their  hands are able to create an edible  garden that they were able to tell how  the this these plants had nourished them  and I hope at my time here at Cornell  that I continue to build these  connections because these connections  aren't singular to young people there's  they are shared between people of all  age groups and I hope to not only build  these connections but build community  thank you  this has been a production of Cornell  University on the web at Cornell edu
 

